# Shell scripts must reach a Linux container with LF endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default, so a plain clone on Windows
# rewrites every checked-out .sh to CRLF. Git's index is unaffected -- the
# blobs stay LF -- but Docker builds from the *working tree*, so the CRLF copy
# is what gets baked into the image, and `#!/bin/sh\r` is not a program:
#
#     exec /home/steam/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# which names a file that is plainly there, with the wrong reason. That cost
# this project a broken test server once already; see testserver/Dockerfile,
# which strips the CR as well so a tree checked out before this file existed
# still builds a working image.
*.sh text eol=lf
